WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.082 --> 00:00:03.670
- We're a big group of strong women

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.300
that takes risks riding motorcycles

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.796
all the time in the City,

00:00:06.796 --> 00:00:09.717
which takes a set of steel
ovaries, in my opinion.

00:00:09.717 --> 00:00:11.844
But, we want to help babies.

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:13.055
Who says no to babies?

00:00:13.055 --> 00:00:15.805
(dramatic music)

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:18.976
(gentle music)

00:00:18.976 --> 00:00:21.559
The club delivers
processed and pasteurized

00:00:21.559 --> 00:00:24.482
donor breast milk to
mothers and babies in need,

00:00:24.482 --> 00:00:28.032
both to NICUs in hospitals
and to private homes.

00:00:28.032 --> 00:00:30.822
We focus our service on
women's health issues,

00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:35.532
so this is a complete fit for
what we try to do as a club.

00:00:35.532 --> 00:00:37.870
The call for milk can come at any time.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.119
You can be anywhere.

00:00:39.119 --> 00:00:41.162
We pull up to the dock at
the New York Milk Bank.

00:00:41.162 --> 00:00:42.078
- Hi!

00:00:42.078 --> 00:00:43.250
- [Jennifer] Julie brings out the milk

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:47.292
that's been pre-packaged
in freezer bags and boxes.

00:00:47.292 --> 00:00:51.125
We strap it down to the
motorcycles, zip away.

00:00:52.131 --> 00:00:53.839
- When we opened up the Milk Bank,

00:00:53.839 --> 00:00:56.098
I was actually stuck in
traffic with my husband

00:00:56.098 --> 00:00:57.970
and saw a motorcycle rider

00:00:57.970 --> 00:00:59.972
illegally driving up the center lane.

00:00:59.972 --> 00:01:02.559
And I thought why can't
we use motorcyclists

00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:05.435
to deliver milk in and out of New York?

00:01:05.435 --> 00:01:09.066
We collect it from women that
have an excess amount of milk.

00:01:09.066 --> 00:01:12.819
We process it, test it, and
distribute it to hospitals

00:01:12.819 --> 00:01:16.986
for premature infants and
to the community at large.

00:01:18.369 --> 00:01:19.702
- Up, good girl.

00:01:20.622 --> 00:01:22.955
Marlowe was born four months early.

00:01:22.955 --> 00:01:26.791
I brought Marlowe home
after 161 days in the NICU.

00:01:26.791 --> 00:01:29.125
I stopped producing breast milk.

00:01:29.125 --> 00:01:32.378
And all of Marlowe's
doctors required Marlowe

00:01:32.378 --> 00:01:35.092
to continue on breast milk

00:01:35.092 --> 00:01:37.799
because putting her on formula

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:40.176
would gravely endanger her life.

00:01:40.176 --> 00:01:42.388
I had to find a way to be able

00:01:42.388 --> 00:01:47.020
to give my daughter breast
milk and I found donor milk.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:49.065
Since then, we've been getting deliveries

00:01:49.065 --> 00:01:50.191
from the Milk Bank.

00:01:50.191 --> 00:01:52.066
We get delivery once a month.

00:01:52.066 --> 00:01:54.816
It's 330 bottles of three ounces.

00:01:55.695 --> 00:01:59.864
The sound of those motorcycles
is the sound of hope.

00:01:59.864 --> 00:02:00.697
Hi!

00:02:01.617 --> 00:02:04.534
They're bringing life, liquid life,

00:02:06.001 --> 00:02:09.084
for a small baby who they don't know.

00:02:12.085 --> 00:02:14.173
Every time we give Marlowe a bottle,

00:02:14.173 --> 00:02:16.465
I start to think about what's in there.

00:02:16.465 --> 00:02:18.595
It's not just one woman's work.

00:02:18.595 --> 00:02:21.890
I know the hard work, energy, labor,

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:26.645
love, dedication and sacrifice
that goes into every ounce.

00:02:26.645 --> 00:02:29.309
We don't waste a drop around here.

00:02:29.309 --> 00:02:30.816
It's priceless.

00:02:30.816 --> 00:02:33.733
(uplifting music)

